meta {
  name: Activate curriculum
  type: http
  seq: 21
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/curricula/{{curriculumId}}
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  X-School-Id: {{schoolCode}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "status": "active",
    "description": "Syllabus as taught this session. Approved by the HOD."
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.status: eq active
}

docs {
  At most one active curriculum per academic session, subject and grade level.
  A second one is 409 curriculum_active_exists, and the message says to archive
  the first: two active syllabuses for one class is two answers to "what are
  they meant to be taught", and every report built on top would have to pick
  one without being told how.

  Archiving is how a syllabus is retired. Deleting is for the one that was
  created by mistake, which is what requests 28 and 29 show.

  code, academic_session_id, subject_id and grade_level_id are refused here
  with 422 rather than applied. They are what the curriculum is.
}
